.research/260729_curator-go-to-csk-parity-delta.md:206:- Security invariants: audit before compiler; immutable/protected cache; no package-controlled args/env/output name; no output execution during install; compiler-free dry-run.
LOGBOOK.md:421:### 1609 — A compiled-status plan may be frozen and replayed only for evidence the planner does not read; protected-cache state is not that
LOGBOOK.md:424:- FINDING: the planner *does* read protected-cache evidence — `cache.Inspect` at `plan.go:504-509`, embedded into the planned facts at `plan.go:521-528` → `factsOf` (`cmd/curator/builds.go:173-190`). `recheckBuildCache` (`builds.go:241-262`) re-takes that lookup and `statusReport` (`cmd/curator/main.go:795-808`) overwrites the classified state with `build-state-changed` on any difference. Replaying a pre-tamper plan over moved cache state therefore publishes `build-state-changed`, never the case's own code.
LOGBOOK.md:425:- ROOT CAUSE of the cycle-1 audit defect: the permission case at reviewed-snapshot `cmd/curator/status_test.go:523-539` (`chmod 0o777` on cache entries) was grouped with the marker cases. `0o777` trips the `stat.Mode & 0o022` boundary test (`internal/buildcache/protection_unix.go:239,259`), flipping the inspected outcome from `cache-hit` to untrusted provenance (`internal/buildcache/cache.go:167-168`). All **three** protected-cache mutations need a plan acquired after their own tamper, not two.
LOGBOOK.md:464:- FINDING: R3 incorrectly assigns `TestStatusReportsCompiledCurrentnessAndFailsCheck`'s protected-cache permission case (`cmd/curator/status_test.go:523-539` in the audited `4c2339dd…` snapshot) to a pre-tamper frozen plan. `planOne` records cache evidence, `recheckBuildCache` re-inspects it, and `statusReport` converts changed evidence to `build-state-changed`; the candidate's cache-window test proves the same `0700`→`0777` move has exactly that result. Preserving the intended `untrusted-build-cache` assertion requires a third post-tamper live plan.
LOGBOOK.md:465:- REQUIRED: revise the audit to classify all three protected-cache mutations as live-plan cases and reconcile its 19→8 count by explicitly combining the clean `--json --check` call, or report 19→9 and the lower savings. The corrected failing-load projection still exceeds 90 seconds.
LOGBOOK.md:471:- ROOT CAUSE: two product mechanisms own essentially all `cmd/curator` wall time, and neither memoizes. (1) Every CLI invocation against a scope with a compiled command runs `planBuilds` (`internal/install/plan.go:363`) -> `Probe`/`Establish` -> `godriver.establish` (`internal/godriver/session.go:157`), which runs three `go` subprocesses and then `fingerprintToolchain` (`internal/godriver/fingerprint.go:34`) over the whole GOROOT — **233 MB / 14,502 files, re-opened and SHA-256'd** — and `Session.Close` (`session.go:332`) fingerprints it a *second* time via `VerifyToolchain`. `Probe` is documented as not memoizing (`session.go:140`). (2) `bootstrapEnvironment` (`session.go:404`) points `GOCACHE` at the operation-private root, so every real compiled install compiles from an empty build cache.
LOGBOOK.md:525:### 1131 — Only protected cache state is observable by the read-only plan; markers and context are not
LOGBOOK.md:527:- FINDING: the currentness verdict is derived from two independent sources, and which one a state comes from decides whether a CLI test can reuse an already acquired plan. `buildReport.CacheOutcome` is `facts.Outcome`, taken from `install.PlannedBuild` (`cmd/curator/builds.go:173`), so the read-only plan itself inspects the protected cache. Install markers and installed-directory contents are read only during classification (`classifySkillBuilds`, `contextExposure`, `cmd/curator/builds.go:345`).
LOGBOOK.md:530:- RESULT: focused `TestGlobalStatus*` coverage run 110.541s -> 43.022s; compiled-scope plans 26 -> 8; real compiled installs 4 -> 2. Two cache cases now snapshot and restore protected cache bytes and permission bits instead of running a real reinstall as fixture cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md:604:- DECISION: the refusal is asymmetric on purpose. Keeping a valid unreferenced entry is always safe (the sweep takes it); restoring an unusable predecessor over an entry a recovered commit points at turns a reported failure into a broken install. `Result.BuildCacheRetained` carries that case out so `repairNotices` never repeats "the live build cache is unchanged" when it is not.
LOGBOOK.md:716:- ANOMALY: this suite is disk-hungry enough to look like a product defect. A `-race` sweep with ~9 GiB free filled the disk and three `internal/install` tests failed with `no space left on device` surfaced through `Result.Errors` as an ordinary installation failure — it reads exactly like a transaction-journal bug. The Go build cache alone reached 8.9 GiB. CI needs a free-space floor. Relevant to `TASK-260720-1pvfj5`.
LOGBOOK.md:879:- FIX: project and global target staging now pass independently derived raw-snapshot validation, protected-cache inspection, cloned planned inputs, and complete static context/runtime file sets. `stageNode` forwards that single proof into `marker.Current`; nodes without compiled commands retain the legacy call shape.
LOGBOOK.md:922:### 0400 — A corrupt protected build cache entry used to brick install permanently
LOGBOOK.md:1299:- ROOT CAUSE: identical message on both trees — `prepare protected cache root: untrusted cache provenance: ... DACL is not protected from inheritance`. `ensureProtectedBase` creates a directory and applies its protected DACL in two steps, so a concurrent publisher observes the gap. Owned by `TASK-260720-3pwg2w`; untouched by this task.
LOGBOOK.md:1413:- MILESTONE: `TASK-260720-1ljev5` — maintenance GC extended to immutable build cache entries. New `internal/buildcache/collect.go` (`Sweep`), a shared mark phase plus `Collect` in `internal/scopes/gc.go`, `openProtectedDir`/`openProtectedChildFile` on all three protection backends, and `cmd/curator gc` now locked and recovery-first.
LOGBOOK.md:1646:- FIX: `Global` was missing MCP verification and registry-attestation resolution entirely, so a machine-wide build could establish the toolchain, inspect the protected cache, and compile before either gate. Both now run in the project order — MCP after the dependency checks, registry after audit, both above `BuildDeps.resolve` — through the shared `mcpVerifier` helper so the two scopes cannot drift. Global's MCP surface is `{ProjectRoot: GlobalRoot(home), UserHome: userHome}`. Global markers carry the evidence instead of `nil, nil`.
LOGBOOK.md:1677:- FIX (R2): `planOne` wraps the protected-cache lookup in `buildsource.Token.Use`, so a reuse verdict is rechecked immediately before and after the decision; `BuildPlan.recheckSources` then rechecks every planned source once, lexically by node name, inside `Verify`. A raced lookup now fails inside read-only planning, and a source that moves after its own bracket is caught before handoff. `internal/install/plan.go:193,340`.
LOGBOOK.md:1688:- REQUIRED: finalize/revalidate toolchain and every frozen source before `OnStaged` or the first shared mutation, retain cleanup ownership separately, and add mutation-injection regressions proving the prior project/global install, consumer ledger, runtime, and live build cache remain unchanged.
.research/260729_install-race-timeouts.md:1206:build cache lives in `~/Library/Caches/go-build` and `GOTMPDIR` is task-owned outside the worktree,
.planning/260720_055300_protocol-schema-v6-decomposition.md:61:- No unresolved product or architecture choice remains: the accepted research contract fixes schema 6, `go-v1`, protocol `1.0.0-rc.4`, marker v2, receipt v1, claim v2, static build-root exclusion, protected cache provenance, and manager-home transaction isolation.
