The first implementation run exposed a real Darwin constraint, not a product-model conflict: `renameatx_np(RENAME_EXCL)` refuses to move a source directory once that directory is mode `0500`. The safe POSIX sequence is to keep the already-complete private staged directory owner-writable, atomically no-replace rename it under the held home lock, then seal the entry directory to `0500` before releasing the lock; all files and the artifact directory are already read-only before rename. Readers fail closed during that tiny sealing window, and competing publishers retry rather than adopt it. I’m adjusting the implementation and tests remain unchanged.
