Strict mypy is green in the isolated task environment. Before treating that as gate evidence, I’m tightening two publication-edge regressions I found in review: malformed source bytes must raise the stable cache error (not a constructor `TypeError`), and dry-run disposition for corrupt candidates needs to match the protocol’s rebuild semantics.
